  "observations": {
    "outline": "All eleven read as warm-brown hand-drawn contours. Bear and Meerkat are somewhat firmer; Siamese and Hedgehog are softer. At the declared display scale these are natural variations, not heavy sticker-like or unnaturally thin outliers.",
    "face": "Mammals share a friendly oval-eye and rounded muzzle construction. Siamese blue irises are an intentional species trait. The three birds share simple small eyes and clean beaks; forcing mammal eyes onto them would reduce series consistency.",
    "texture": "All use warm watercolor/paper texture. Siamese/Meerkat grain is more apparent in the source view, but remains restrained and harmonious at the intended display scale.",
    "palette": "Cream, sand, rust and warm brown remain coherent; pink Rabbit, natural green/blue/red Pitta and white Onagadori retain distinct species/character identity without a palette mismatch.",
    "proportions": "Long rabbit ears, slender Meerkat neck, three-quarter Kangaroo head and long Onagadori tail are intentional species differences. Body-based scale retains ears and excludes tail width from the scaling basis.",
    "alpha": "Cream and dark-teal composites show no visible matte, checkerboard, colored halo or clipped feet/ears/tail. Native black transparency can overemphasize extremely low-alpha RGB; acceptance is based on proper alpha composites."
  },
